/target
.DS_Store

# Design reference screenshots stay local: ten frames at ~90KB each is a lot of
# history for files whose usefulness ends when the decision is made. They are also
# mockups of the v1 design rather than captures of this program, so they describe a
# UI that no longer exists.
#
# The logo is different. `include_bytes!` pulls it in at compile time, so it is a
# build input, not a reference: without it a fresh clone does not compile. The
# directory has to be excluded with a wildcard rather than by name, because git
# will not re-include a file inside an excluded directory.
#
# `screens/` is tracked for the same reason as the logo, one step removed: the
# README embeds it, so a clone without it renders with broken images. Captures of
# the running program, not mockups — the distinction the paragraph above is about.
/assets/*
!/assets/flutter-trim.png
!/assets/flutter.png
!/assets/screens/
!/assets/screens/*.png
